# Docker, nginx and shell tooling are line-ending sensitive and these files ship
# to a Linux VM. With core.autocrlf=true (default on Windows) a fresh clone
# would otherwise rewrite them as CRLF in the working tree, and that CRLF copy
# is what Docker sends in the build context.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the deployment files instead of a blanket
# "* text=auto": a global rule would renormalize every existing (CRLF)
# application file and produce a huge, unrelated diff.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.env* text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
